    {
      "step_id": "tile_data_shape_and_types.s02",
      "type": "explainer",
      "concept_ids": [
        "data.dataset_rows_columns"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Rows and Columns",
      "title": "Rows are observations; columns are variables",
      "lede": "The two directions of the table mean different things — and knowing which is which is the first skill in reading any dataset.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_data_shape_and_types.s02.b01",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "text": "Each row represents one observation — one record. In the Kwik Courier data that means one row per delivery: order #1042 is one row, order #1043 is the next row, and so on. Each column represents one variable: one attribute that is recorded for every observation in the dataset. The city column holds the destination city for every single delivery; the delivery_min column holds the delivery time for every single delivery. Each column carries just one kind of information.",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb3"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f3",
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_data_shape_and_types.s02.b02",
          "role": "example",
          "text": "Reading the table this way tells you exactly how to answer a question about it. Asked \"how many deliveries went to Lagos?\", you scan down the city column and count matching rows. Asked \"what happened with order #1042?\", you look across that one row and read every column. The row tells you about one delivery; the column tells you about one kind of fact across all deliveries.",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb4"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f3",
              "data.dataset_rows_columns#f4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "reward": {
        "gems": 2
      },
      "lineage": {
        "concept_ids": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns"
        ],
        "teaching_block_ids": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb3",
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#tb4"
        ],
        "fact_ids": [
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#f3",
          "data.dataset_rows_columns#f4"
        ]
      }
    },
